nsiproxy: find network interfaces by index on Haiku too

find_entry_from_index() always returned NULL on Haiku (a Haiku patch,
reason not recorded), so update_if_table() appended every interface
again at each call: the interface table grew between two calls, and
GetAdaptersInfo() never succeeded (its size from the first call was
always too small for the second, ERROR_BUFFER_OVERFLOW forever), and
convert_index_to_luid() never found an interface. Look the index up as
on the other systems (Haiku's if_nameindex() indices are stable).
Found with Need for Speed: Porsche Unleashed (W11), whose local address
comes from gethostbyname(), which Wine builds from GetAdaptersInfo().

--- a/dlls/nsiproxy.sys/ndis.c
+++ b/dlls/nsiproxy.sys/ndis.c
@@ -107,17 +107,12 @@
 
 static struct if_entry *find_entry_from_index( UINT index )
 {
-#ifdef __HAIKU__
-    return NULL;
-#else
-
     struct if_entry *entry;
 
     LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( entry, &if_list, struct if_entry, entry )
         if (entry->if_index == index) return entry;
 
     return NULL;
-#endif
 }
 
 static struct if_entry *find_entry_from_luid( const NET_LUID *luid )
